module bindings.cpp.unbounded_call_sized_stack_array;

// A variable-length array's size is evaluated when the frame is laid out,
// so `unsigned char buf[n]` claims n bytes of stack for whatever n holds
// at that point. When n is the length a received-data API reports -- the
// byte count of a payload a peer sent -- the sender chooses the size of
// the receiver's stack allocation, and a message large enough exhausts
// it. The bound the allocation needs is a comparison on that length
// before it sizes the array, which is the fix shape everywhere this
// family lands: reject the oversized value and return. The Zenoh uORB
// handlers carrying this shape are C++ headers, so the C++ corpus needs
// the binding as much as the C one.
//
// The fact is emitted by the shared C-family frontend
// (ccUnboundedCallSizedStackArrayObservations,
// internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go) from the syntax tree: the
// array declarator's size must be a bare identifier, that identifier
// must last be assigned from a call in the same function, and any
// relational comparison naming it, in either operand order, clears the
// fact, so a clamp, an early return and the mirrored spellings all read
// as consulting it while a comparison of an unrelated value leaves it
// standing. An equality check does not clear: the compacted text cannot
// tell an exact-match fix from an error-sentinel check (`len == 0`), and
// a sentinel must not vouch for a bound. The observation is
// callee-neutral and carries the callee in the fact, so which calls
// report a received length is decided here, in data: today zenoh-pico's
// z_bytes_len, the documented byte count of the payload a sample
// carries. The next library's spelling is a binding edit, not an engine
// change -- an unrestricted callee list was measured at eighteen sites
// across three trees of which one was received data, the rest sizing
// stacks from config, list and macro arithmetic.
//
// Residuals, all false-negative: the comparison is not required to
// precede the allocation, so a check after the declaration vouches for
// it, and one in a sibling branch vouches for every array in the
// function; the compacted body keeps comments, so a commented-out bound
// still clears; and an identifier a non-call later overwrites stops
// qualifying even when the call's value is the one the array used. The
// equality residual runs the other way: a fix that pins the length by
// equality against the expected size still reports.
binding unboundedCallSizedStackArray {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.kind == "any" and node.analysis == "alloc.unbounded_call_sized_stack_array" and containsAny(node.token, ["callee=z_bytes_len"])
  emit issue code.UnboundedCallSizedStackArray at node
}
